From bf82889c939e6cb96e7af327d74d6e08d6409269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:21:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(ui): show the machine overview as a two-column
 property grid

The Machine page and the machine editor header printed
Machine::summary() as one run-on sentence with bare `?` for unknown
values. Add Machine::rows(unit), label/value rows (Kind, Machine,
Spindle, Axes with each stroke, Tool changer, Coolant, Workspace;
"not stated" for unknowns, lengths in the document unit), and draw them
as a wrapping egui Grid on both. The page adds a Source row.
summary() is unchanged for the setup sheet and boundary_draft.

Fixes #745

